// m_gladiator.c -- the GLADIATOR monster (2023 Quake II re-release / "KEX"
// engine). Ported from ~/Projects/quake2-rerelease-dll/rerelease/
// m_gladiator.cpp (488 lines, C++17) + m_gladiator.h (101 lines, frame index
// constants, "This file generated by ModelGen - Do NOT Modify"): the full
// stand/walk/run/melee(cleaver)/railgun-attack/pain/death frame-animation
// system, gladiator_pain/gladiator_die/gladiator_setskin/gladiator_blocked,
// and the RAFAEL (Ground Zero mission-pack) `monster_gladb` variant baked
// directly into this base-game file by KEX (distinct health/mass/skin/
// power-armor/weapon-sound stats, a `self->style` flag, and its own
// gladb-specific plasma-gun attack move). Behavioral code, ported bug-for-bug
// per PORTING.md.
//
// ============================================================================
// EXTERNAL DEPENDENCIES NOT YET PORTED (throwing stubs, cited)
// ============================================================================
// - `fire_plasma(self, start, dir, damage, speed, damage_radius,
//   radius_damage)`: declared in g_local.h:2339 but its ONLY body in the
//   whole rerelease source tree lives in
//   ~/Projects/quake2-rerelease-dll/rerelease/xatrix/g_xatrix_weapon.cpp:280
//   -- xatrix (Ground Zero's sibling mission pack) weapon content, out of
//   scope for this base-game monster porting round (no src/kexgame/
//   g_xatrix_weapon.ts exists). Only `gladbGun`/`gladbGun_check` (the
//   RAFAEL/gladb-only attack) reach this, so a base `monster_gladiator`
//   (self->style !== 1) never calls it. `monster_gladb` genuinely throws if
//   it ever fires its plasma gun today -- an honest gap, not a silent
//   behavior change, mirroring g_turret.ts's own `infantry_die`-family stub
//   precedent for the identical kind of missing-content-dir gap.
// - `blocked_checkplat(self, dist)`: declared in g_local.h:2544 but its ONLY
//   body in the whole rerelease source tree lives in
//   ~/Projects/quake2-rerelease-dll/rerelease/rogue/g_rogue_newai.cpp:14 --
//   rogue (Ground Zero) AI content, likewise out of scope here. Every
//   `monsterinfo.blocked` handler in the base game calls it (not
//   gladiator-specific), so `gladiator_blocked` genuinely throws if a plat
//   ever blocks this monster's path today.
//
// ============================================================================
// PLACEMENT-MISMATCH FUNCTIONS PORTED LOCALLY
// ============================================================================
// - `monster_footstep(edict_t*)` (g_local.h:3282, `inline`, `[Paril-KEX]`):
//   `self->s.event = EV_OTHER_FOOTSTEP` if grounded. Trivial one-liner,
//   reimplemented locally rather than imported -- same treatment m_flipper.ts
//   gives `M_CheckGib` (see that file's header): declared in g_local.h, not
//   g_monster.cpp, so no earlier kexgame unit had a reason to port it yet.
// - `M_CheckGib(edict_t*, const mod_t&)` (g_local.h:3521, `inline`):
//   `self->deadflag && mod.id == MOD_CRUSH` short-circuits true, else
//   `self->health <= self->gib_health`. Reimplemented locally for the same
//   reason -- identical body to m_flipper.ts's own local copy.
//
// ============================================================================
// DEVIATIONS
// ============================================================================
// - `M_SetAnimation`'s C++ declaration (g_local.h:2211) defaults `instant` to
//   `true`; every call site in this file omits the arg, so every call here
//   passes `true` explicitly (TS has no default for this positional param
//   the way this codebase ports it elsewhere -- matching m_flipper.ts's own
//   `M_SetAnimation(self, move, true)` calls).
// - `cached_soundindex` fields port as plain per-file `let sound_x = 0`
//   module variables reassigned in `SP_monster_gladiator`, matching
//   m_flipper.ts's exact precedent (not g_trigger.ts's `{ index: 0 }` box,
//   which predates this simpler sibling convention).
// - `mframe_t`/`mmove_t` construction uses the local `frame()`/`move()`
//   helpers, matching m_flipper.ts's precedent exactly (MframeT is a plain
//   interface; MmoveT's frame-count validation happens in its `frame`
//   setter, so `move()` must assign `firstframe`/`lastframe` before `frame`).
// - Vec3 "copy" sites (`self->pos1 = self->enemy->s.origin`-shaped C++
//   value-semantics assignments) use `vec3(v[0], v[1], v[2])`, matching
//   g_turret.ts's own established idiom -- a `Vec3` is a mutable
//   `Float32Array`; a bare `=` would alias instead of copy.
// - `self->enemy` (nullable in `EdictT`) is narrowed via an explicit
//   `if (enemy === null) return` guard at the top of every function that
//   dereferences it, rather than a non-null assertion -- no casts anywhere
//   in this file besides `as const`.
// - `st` (spawn_temp_t) is the real, shared singleton imported from the
//   landed g_spawn.ts.

